I can confirm this behavior. I uploaded the latest stable OpenGD77 version to an RT3S from 07/2024. I now have two RT3S devices—one from 2023 and a newer one from 2024.<br><br>On 430 MHz, when in DMR mode, transmitting from the older device to the newer one works fine. However, when I transmit from the newer device, the transmission becomes garbled after about 3 seconds when received by the older device. Both devices are running the same firmware and codeplug.<br><br>Transmitting in DMR mode works fine in both directions on 439 MHz.<br><br>When I enable the "Signal" menu option in the firmware, I observe that the signal from the older device to the newer one is stable. In the other direction, the signal fluctuates wildly.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8619">SP8AC</a> — Sat May 17, 2025 9:27 pm</p><hr />
