Hi all,<br><br>I think I have the same issue with my DM-1701A's. Everything works well except DMR around 430-435 Mhz with OpenGD77. VHF, &lt; 420 Mhz, &gt; 439 Mhz and FM are all okay. I'm using version 20250323054354 [ 1bd23ea D ].<br><br>I've tried different antennas, different timeslots, filters, mic gain, eco level, no TA, CRC is on. I installed the original firmware to make sure it isn't a hardware issue as these are new from AliExpress, so you never know. It didn't have this issue, though I must say after experiencing OpenGD77, the stock firmware sucks <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> <br><br>It was clear the issue is transmitting, since going from stock to OpenGD77 worked fine. When receiving the garbled signal the stock firmware keeps dropping the call like it's getting out of sync or something.<br><br>Let me know if there is anything I can do to help debug.<br><br>73 KC1WSW<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8568">KC1WSW</a> — Sat May 17, 2025 4:52 pm</p><hr />
